PyTorch master (d8729ef) Apr 23, 2019. (Also present in 1.0.0 and 1.0.1)
The copy from x to y should be non-blocking. It's not because _s_copy_from_cuda drops the non_blocking argument.
import torch

x = torch.randn(10, device='cuda')
y = torch.empty(10, pin_memory=True)
y.copy_(x, non_blocking=True)



      pytorch/aten/src/ATen/native/cuda/Copy.cu


        Lines 298 to 305
      in
      e9c8f37







           Tensor _s_copy_from_cuda( 




               const Tensor& self, 




               const Tensor& dst, 




               bool non_blocking) { 




             Tensor dst_ = dst; 




             _s_copy__cuda(dst_, self); 




             return dst; 




           }

